message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HGT-Scheduler: Exploiting Edge Semantics in Job Shop Scheduling Problem with Heterogeneous Graph Transformers"
authors:
  - family-names: Soykan
    given-names: Bulent
    email: Bulent.Soykan@ucf.edu
    affiliation: "Institute for Simulation and Training, University of Central Florida"
    orcid: ""
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-03-06
abstract: >
  A reinforcement learning scheduler for the Job Shop Scheduling Problem (JSSP)
  that uses a Heterogeneous Graph Transformer (HGT) to exploit the two distinct
  edge semantics of the disjunctive graph representation: precedence constraints
  ('precedes' edges) and machine-sharing contention ('competes' edges).
  Type-dependent attention over these edge types yields a statistically significant
  improvement on the FT06 benchmark (p=0.011) over a homogeneous ablation baseline.
keywords:
  - job shop scheduling
  - heterogeneous graph transformer
  - reinforcement learning
  - PPO
  - graph neural network
  - disjunctive graph
